!______________________________________________________________________________
! B.W. Weber, W.J. Pitz., M. Mehl, E.J. Silke, A.C. Davis, C.J. Sung, Combust. Flame, 2014, 161, 1972-1983 
!Compared with MCH
C8ENE-ONE + OH  = C8ENE-ONEJ + H2O               3.00E+06  1.8   1300.0     ! Analogy with ch3cho+oh, A*1.5 Taylor et al. Proc. Comb. Symp., 26, p. 497-504 (1996)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
C8ENE-ONE + HO2 = C8ENE-ONEJ + H2O2              4.82E+03  2.6   13910.0    ! Analogy with ch3cho+ho2, from Curran et al. 2004, C3_31 mech                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 
C8ENE-ONE + H   = C8ENE-ONEJ + H2                1.34E+13  0.0   3300.0     ! Assume rate rule for aldehydic H from nc7_38 LLNL mech, (ch3cho+h from Whytock et al. J. Chem. Phys. 65 (1976).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     
C8ENE-ONE + CH3 = C8ENE-ONEJ + CH4               1.34E+13  0.0   3300.0     ! Assume rate rule for aldehydic H from nc7_38 LLNL mech                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       
C8ENE-ONE + OH  = C8ENEJ-ONE + H2O               3.17E+06  2.00 -1434.0     ! Rate rule for secondary Allylic H, Heyberger et al., Oxidation of Small Alkenes, IJCK 34:666-677 2002). Estimated uncertainty factor = 1.5
C8ENE-ONE + HO2 = C8ENEJ-ONE + H2O2              6.80E+03  2.50  10113.8    ! Rate rule for seconary allylic H, Scott and Walker, Addition of Toluene, COMBUSTION AND FLAME 129:365?377 (2002).  Estimated based on ethylbenzene+ho2                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    
C8ENE-ONE + H   = C8ENEJ-ONE + H2                5.02E+04  2.50 -1912.0     ! Rate rule for secondary Allylic H, Heyberger et al., Oxidation of Small Alkenes, IJCK 34:666-677 2002). Estimated uncertainty factor = 1.5                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             
C8ENE-ONE + CH3 = C8ENEJ-ONE + CH4               1.47      3.50  4046.1     ! WJP: About factor of 15 error in the A-factor in Table 1 of  Heyberger et al. log A = -0.13 not -1.3                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             
C8ENE-ONEJ => CO+C3H6+C4H71-2                    1.83E+15 -0.73  12910.0    ! Analogy with c2h5co = c2h5+co, Curran et al. C3_31 mech, 2004,reverse rate rule = 1.510E+11exp(-4.810E+03cal/RT)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              
C8ENEJ-ONE = C4H6+C3H6CHO-2                      1.83E+14  0.258 40425.1    ! Analogy with jc8h15-B decomp, Pitz et al., diisobutylene mech, 2004
